            <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl">2. Data Collection on This Website</h2>
            <h3>Server Log Files</h3>
            <p>The provider of this website automatically collects and stores information in server log files, which your browser automatically transmits to us. This information includes: browser type and version, operating system used, referrer URL, host name of the accessing computer, time of the server request, and IP address. This data is not merged with other data sources. The basis for data processing is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, which allows the processing of data to fulfill a contract or for measures preliminary to a contract.</p>

            <h3>Contact Form (via Formspree)</h3>
            <p>If you send us inquiries via the contact form, your details from the inquiry form, including the contact details you provided there, will be stored by us for the purpose of processing the inquiry and in the event of follow-up questions. This data is forwarded to the service Formspree, Inc., 1201 Mariposa St #100, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA, to ensure the functionality of the contact form. The processing of this data is based on Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR; our legitimate interest is to process your request efficiently. For more information, please see Formspree's privacy policy: <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/</a>.</p>

            <h3>Inquiries by E-mail or Telephone</h3>
            <p>If you contact us by e-mail or telephone, your inquiry including all resulting personal data (name, inquiry) will be stored and processed by us for the purpose of processing your request. We do not pass on this data without your consent. The processing of this data is based on Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR, provided that your inquiry is related to the fulfillment of a contract or is necessary for the performance of pre-contractual measures. In all other cases, the processing is based on our legitimate interest in the effective processing of the inquiries addressed to us (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR) or on your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR) if this has been requested.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl">3. Analysis and Marketing Tools</h2>
            <h3>Plausible Analytics</h3>
            <p>This website uses Plausible Analytics, a privacy-friendly web analytics service. The provider is Plausible Insights OÜ, Västriku tn 2, 50403, Tartu, Estonia. Plausible does not use cookies and does not collect personal data. Only anonymized usage statistics are collected, without the possibility of identifying individual users. IP addresses are not stored. The data processing is based on our legitimate interest in the statistical analysis of user behavior for optimization purposes in accordance with Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. For more information, please refer to Plausible's privacy policy: <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://plausible.io/data-policy</a>.</p>

            <h3>Use of Leadfeeder</h3>
            <p>This website uses Leadfeeder, a website-visitor identification service provided by Dealfront Group GmbH, Durlacher Allee 73, 76131 Karlsruhe, Germany, to recognise the companies behind business visits to this website for marketing and optimization purposes on the basis of the website operator's legitimate interests (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).</p>
            <p>For this purpose, a javascript-based code collects usage data and the visitor's IP address, which is matched against a database in order to identify the associated company. A first-party cookie is used to recognise the device across sessions. The data is pseudonymized and is not used to personally identify individual visitors to this website.</p>
            <p>The data collected via Leadfeeder is deleted as soon as it is no longer required for its intended purpose and there are no statutory retention obligations to the contrary.</p>
            <p>You may object to this tracking at any time with effect for the future by enabling the "Do Not Track" setting in your browser, which Leadfeeder honours. Further information is available in Leadfeeder's privacy notice at <a href="https://www.leadfeeder.com/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://www.leadfeeder.com/privacy/</a>.</p>

            <h3>Google Ads Conversion Tracking</h3>
            <p>This website uses Google Ads conversion tracking and the associated Google tag ("gtag.js"), an online advertising service provided by Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland ("Google"), to measure the success of our Google Ads advertising campaigns on the basis of the website operator's legitimate interests (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Our legitimate interest lies in measuring and optimizing the effectiveness of our advertising.</p>
            <p>When you reach our website via an ad served by Google, a conversion tracking cookie is stored on your device. If you subsequently complete a specific action (e.g. submitting the contact form to arrange an appointment), Google and we can recognise that you reached our website via an ad. We learn the total number of users who clicked on one of our ads and completed such an action, but we do not receive any information that could be used to personally identify individual visitors. In this process, data may be transferred to servers of Google LLC in the USA; Google is certified under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework.</p>
            <p>You may object to conversion tracking at any time with effect for the future by disabling cookies in your browser settings or blocking cookies from the domain "googleadservices.com", or by deactivating personalised advertising in Google's ad settings at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://adssettings.google.com</a>.</p>
            <p>For more information on data protection at Google, please refer to Google's privacy policy at <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a>.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl">4. Plugins and Tools</h2>
            <h3>Google Fonts</h3>
            <p>This site uses so-called Google Fonts for the uniform display of fonts, which are provided by Google. When you call up a page, your browser loads the required web fonts into your browser cache in order to display texts and fonts correctly. For this purpose, the browser you are using must connect to Google's servers. This enables Google to know that our website has been accessed via your IP address. The use of Google Fonts is in the interest of a uniform and appealing presentation of our online offers. This constitutes a legitimate interest within the meaning of Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR.</p>

            <h3>Zeeg.me</h3>
            <p>We use the Zeeg.me service for online appointment booking. When you book an appointment, the data you enter (name, email address, etc.) is transmitted to and processed by Zeeg.me. The processing is carried out for the implementation of pre-contractual measures at your request (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR). For more information on data protection at Zeeg.me, please visit: <a href="https://zeeg.me/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://zeeg.me/privacy</a>.</p>

